    Remove commons-lang 2.6 from the ext-core feature (#8216)
    
    No installed bundle imports org.apache.commons.lang, neither mandatorily
    nor optionally nor dynamically. The FIXME assumed the Spring LDAP bundle
    needs it, but only Spring LDAP 1.x depended on commons-lang; the 2.4.1
    bundle we ship does not.
    
    Tested LDAP with and without commons-lang against the public forumsys
    LDAP test server, with identical results: login through LDAP bind
    authentication, rejected logins for a wrong password and an unknown
    user, database login still working, and name, email and roles provided
    by the LDAP user directory. No class loading or wiring errors in the
    logs.
    
    Part of #8214
    
